tyle, slow (≈4 s/req) | Model not suited for narrative style | Discarded, reverted to Gemini |\n| Gemini 3.8‑flash‑low capacity errors (503) | “No capacity available” on large chunks | Server quota exceeded for that model | Implemented adaptive sub‑chunk splitting; reduced concurrency to 15 workers |\n| Prompt block filter (sensitive words) | Gemini blocked some chunks | Prompt contained prohibited terms | Re‑phrased prompts, removed trigger words, kept style rules intact |\n| Artifact naming mismatch (short names) | User requested full names | Original name map used short aliases | Updated name map to full names and edited prompt accordingly |\n| Failed `test_gemini_names.js` (streaming output) | Mis‑handled streaming chunk format | Used wrong model endpoint (`gemini‑3.8‑flash‑control`) | Discarded; relied on final translation output instead |\n| Unnecessary scripts (`audit_names.js`, stress tests) | Left behind temporary files | Created for debugging | Deleted after use |\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- **Running environment:** Local Windows machine, workspace at `C:\\Users\\Eevyx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\dfaefe40-f699-4276-8717-cb4f8030016c`.  \n- **Current artifacts:**  \n  - `translate-novel-dragndrop.ts` (modified with new config & prompt).  \n  - Output novel file (full translation).  \n  - Checkpoint JSON and chunk cache folder (populated).  \n- **Assumptions:** Full‑name map is exhaustive for this novel; any unseen character will default to the name as it appears in source text.  \n- **Dependencies:** None pending; all external calls (9router) succeed under current load.  \n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Create `agents.md`** in the artifact directory:\n   - Header: Project title, date, author (Antigravity).  \n   - **Environment** section: OS, tool versions, 9router endpoint, API key (redacted).  \n   - **Model & Endpoint**: `ag/gemini-3.8-flash-low` via `http://localhost:20128/v1`.  \n   - **Prompt Design**: Include exact prompt text (style description, dialog rules, name map).  \n   - **Configuration**: Show `CONFIG` object (proxyUrl, model, apiKey, maxChunkChars, concurrency).  \n   - **Workflow**: Outline steps – chunking, adaptive sub‑chunk splitting, caching, checkpoint usage, parallel worker handling.  \n   - **Performance Summary**: Table of per‑chapter times, average latency, max concurrency tested (40), chosen 15‑worker setting.  \n   - **Error Handling**: Describe 503 handling, block filter retries, fallback to sub‑chunks.  \n   - **Audit Results**: Insert dialog count, top speakers, % of proper name usage.  \n   - **Future Improvements**: Suggest increasing model capacity, adding more characters to name map, experimenting with higher concurrency, or switching to a higher‑capacity model.  \n2. **Validate `agents.md`**: Open the file, ensure markdown renders correctly (headings, tables, code blocks). No further runtime actions needed.  \n3. **Optional clean‑up**:  \n   - Remove any temporary debug scripts (already deleted).  \n   - Ensure no stray `console.log` statements remain in `translate-novel-dragndrop.ts` (they are harmless but can be left).  \n4. **Deliverable**: Inform user that `agents.md` is ready and provide its location; attach a preview link if needed.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Formatting:** All responses must be concise, markdown‑styled when appropriate, and respect the user’s “full‑name” dialog rule.  \n- **No external calls:** Only local 9router is permitted; avoid any other network requests.  \n- **Security:** Do not expose the API key in public messages; keep it only in the config file.  \n- **User preferences:** Use informal, “gaul” Bahasa Indonesia style in explanations, but keep technical sections clear and formal.  \n- **Promise:** I will produce the `agents.md` file as described, containing all the info above, before any further action is taken.\n\n**Ready to create `agents.md` now.**\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 11 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[AR